# clangd configuration so the editor analyzes our sources the way the build actually compiles them.
# Two project-specific issues make this necessary; without it clangd reports spurious errors
# (unresolved <duckdb/...> includes, "no member ... in duckdb::Storage", #error on our own .cpp files).
#
# 1. compile_commands.json lives in build/release/, which clangd does NOT find on its own. By default it
#    searches the file's directory, its parents, and a `build/` subdirectory of each -- but not the nested
#    `build/release/`. With no compilation database clangd falls back to bare flags (no -I/-isystem), so
#    every angled duckdb include and every src-relative include ("storage/multi_block_writer.hpp") fails.
#    CompilationDatabase (relative to this .clangd file) points clangd at the database, so each file inherits
#    the real -I / -isystem / -D flags the build uses.
#
# 2. Our per-component translation units (ss_table.cpp, ss_table_builder.cpp, memtable.cpp, ...) are unity-
#    build fragments: inverted_index_ub.cpp does `#define INVERTED_INDEX_UNITY_BUILD` and then #includes
#    them, and each fragment starts with `#ifndef INVERTED_INDEX_UNITY_BUILD / #error`. Only the _ub.cpp is
#    in compile_commands.json; clangd analyzes each fragment standalone by inferring flags from that sibling
#    command -- but the macro is a *source* #define, not a compile flag, so it is absent and the #error
#    fires (which also aborts before the includes, cascading into "undeclared identifier" noise). Defining
#    it here lets clangd parse the fragments as the unity build does. The value is left empty to match the
#    bare `#define` in inverted_index_ub.cpp, so the two definitions are identical and clangd does not warn
#    about a macro redefinition when it indexes that file.
#
# Note: this pins indexing to the release configuration. Debug-only blocks guarded by
# `#if defined(D_ASSERT_IS_ENABLED) || !defined(NDEBUG)` will show as inactive in the editor; that is a
# cosmetic indexing choice, not a build effect. Point CompilationDatabase at build/debug if you'd rather
# see those active.
CompileFlags:
  CompilationDatabase: build/release
  Add:
    - -DINVERTED_INDEX_UNITY_BUILD=
